---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { ADS_ENABLED } from '../config/ads';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Disclaimer — 1RMHub"
  h1="Disclaimer"
  description="1RMHub results are estimates, not tested maxes, guaranteed performance or medical advice. Read how to interpret them and lift safely."
  path="/disclaimer/"
  name="Disclaimer"
>
  <p class="answer">
    Every number on {SITE.name} is an <strong>estimate</strong>. It is not a tested maximum, not a
    guarantee of what you can lift, and not medical, health or individual coaching advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Estimates, not guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    One rep max results are calculated from published prediction formulas applied to the set you
    enter. Real performance depends on technique, fatigue, sleep, stress, experience, equipment and
    the exercise itself. Formulas can over- or under-estimate an individual&rsquo;s true max, and they
    become less reliable as the number of reps rises. See the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>
    for the limits of each tool.
  </p>

  <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
  <p>
    The content on this site is general educational information. It does not replace advice from
    a doctor, physiotherapist or other qualified professional. If you have an injury, a medical
    condition, are pregnant, or are unsure whether strength training or maximal lifting is safe for
    you, seek professional advice before you start.
  </p>

  <h2>Lifting carries risk</h2>
  <p>
    Heavy and maximal lifting can cause injury. Use proper technique and suitable equipment, warm up,
    use a spotter or safety arms, and stop if you feel pain, dizziness or anything unusual. Never
    attempt a weight because a calculator suggests you could lift it.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy of content</h2>
  <p>
    We check calculations with automated tests and cite sources for factual claims, but errors are
    possible. If you find one, please <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>. Use of the site is also subject to
    the <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and affiliate links</h2>
  {ADS_ENABLED ? (
    <p>
      {SITE.name} shows ads served by Google AdSense, labelled &ldquo;Advertisement&rdquo;. It contains
      no affiliate links. Advertisers have no influence over the content, and ads never affect how
      anything is calculated. See the <a href="/privacy/#advertising">privacy policy</a> for how ads use cookies.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      {SITE.name} currently contains no advertising and no affiliate links. If that changes, ads and
      affiliate links will be clearly identified, and they will never affect how anything is calculated.
    </p>
  )}
</LegalLayout>
